      "from": {
       "kind": "agent"
      },
      "text": "I found where the chip takes its colour. It reads `mergeLineTone` in `merge-line.ts` and the tone comes from the pull request's `mergeable` field alone.\n\n## What I will change\n\n- Read `behind_by` from the record as well\n- Keep green only when `behind_by` is `0`\n- Show amber for a stale branch, with the tooltip `Behind main`\n\n```rust\nfn tone(pr: &Pull) -> Tone {\n    if pr.behind_by > 0 { Tone::Amber } else { Tone::Green }\n}\n```\n\nThis leaves **red** for a failed Check alone. Tell me if you want the stale state to take another colour."
     }
